      "extract": "The Ising model is a mathematical model of ferro-magnetism in statistical physics. It was introduced in 1920 by Wilhelm Lenz who gave it as a problem to his Ph.D. student Ernst Ising [@Ising]. It can be defined on any finite graph, but we restrict ourselves to finite subsets $\\Lambda$ of $\\mathbb{Z}^d$. For any lattice site $i \\in \\Lambda$, there is a random variable $\\sigma_i$ which is equal to either $1$ or $-1$",
      "extractCut": true
